      p_problem_descr          => 'Payment accounting is incorrect due to incorrect final pay rounding when there exsists an exchange rate variance (ERV) for an invoice price variance (IPV). This can cause fully paid invoices to appear on the trial balance<br/><strong>Impact Area(s): </strong>Accounting Incorrect, Trial Balance',
      p_solution               => '<strong>Bug Number: </strong>13043111</br><strong>Note: </strong>[1453591/KB594820]</br><strong>Script Name: </strong>ap_fpr_erv_for_ipv.sql</br></br>Apply the root cause fix from bug {13043111} if you have not done so, and log a Service Request to obtain the data fix.</br></br><strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> This fix will undo accounting.<br/><br/>'||mask_text(g_apply_undo, nvl( upper(''), 'NO_MASK') )||'<strong>NOTE:</strong>For transactions posted in <strong>closed periods</strong> the reversing and corrected events will be accounted <strong>in the current open period.</strong><br/>For a deeper understanding of the undo accounting process please refer to [753695/KB218158]</br>',
